s, and reviewed translation into constraints without inventing thresholds. | Specified Narrative/coverage records and modality rules in Ch. 3 and Core 0. Apple note and cross-reference obligations are retained; representative debt language is interpreted. Complete translation of all material narratives remains open. G2, G11. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-58-| MC04 | Separate reported assertions, extraction readings, derivations, assumptions and conflicts. U1, U2, P, D. | Define source/derived/assumed status propagation and conflict handling; show both extraction error and a genuinely conflicting disclosure without silently changing either source. | Specified source/assumption constraints, review actions and conflict sets in Chs. 3, 6, 10. The 720-to-120 OCR repair differs from the 120-to-110 reported correction; transitive invalidation has a reference check. Bounded debt acceptance/source/assumption links are now checked; full workflow validation remains pending. G2, G15, G17. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:59:| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:60:| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-61-| MC07 | Align differing company labels and overlapping dimensions without equating unlike measurements or double counting. U1, D. | Specify concept/mapping relationships, applicability and aggregation rules; demonstrate company extensions and product/geography totals over the same population. | Specified mapping composition, applicability and partition obligations in Ch. 3/Core 0. The product/channel overlap counterexample is checked; general company-extension/mapping validation awaits implementation. G2, G12. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-62-\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-63-## M2 — Histories, interpretation and uncertainty\n--\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-74-\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-75-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-76-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:77:| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event preconditions and operations in Chs. 2, 8. Reference journals, atomic rejection and idempotency checks pass. This verifies the bounded oracle, not a production event engine or accounting compliance. G2, G4, G6. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-78-| MC14 | Give scenarios and decision information explicit meanings. U2, P, D. | Define supported exogenous stress, observational-conditioning and intervention modes, or explicitly scope unsupported modes; enforce information dates and distinguish real-world from pricing measures. | Specified exogenous stress, observational conditioning, intervention preconditions and information capabilities in Ch. 8/Core 0. Finite conditioning, an information-date example and debt stress typing/provenance are checked; causal intervention execution and arbitrary information-policy enforcement remain pending. G6, G14. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:79:| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:80:| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:81:| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-82-| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-83-\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-84-## M4 — Standards, sectors and company variation\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-85-\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-86-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md-87-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:88:| MC19 | A