{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -C 5 'MC06|MC15|MC17|MC19|MC29|MC30|G4|G7|G8' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\"","aggregated_output":"54-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n55-| MC01 | Account for complete annual, quarterly and semi-annual disclosure packages, including notes and relevant referenced material. U1, U3. | Define the source inventory, coverage units, cross-reference closure and disposition rules. A worked filing package must account for retained, structured, duplicated and unresolved content without treating page extraction as semantic completion. | Specified procedure; acquired-file inventory checked. Ch. 2 Apple and Ch. 3 coverage; `cases/apple/manifest.json` accounts for 121 annual pages, 13 annual notes and 10 interim notes. External incorporated documents and full semantic translation remain incomplete. G5, G11. The added source corpus now has 192 checked annual/interim files across nine issuers and 2018–2025; incorporated-package closure and semantic annotation remain open. |\n56-| MC02 | Preserve numeric meaning: entities, perimeter, concept, dimensions, currency, units, scale, sign, basis and precision. U1, D. | Complete context/value types and compatibility rules, with valid/invalid examples and faithful rendering of the original disclosed amounts. | Specified in Chs. 3, 7 and Core 0 Context/Domain/Posting records, including display and rounding metadata. Schema, source scales and rounded-debt calculations have bounded checks; bounded debt context/type/source-binding checks and schema-valid rejection cases now pass. General context/type validation remains incomplete. G2, G3, G12. |\n57-| MC03 | Represent narrative policies, qualifications, commitments and cross-references, including material that is not executable yet. U1, U3, D. | Specify narrative assertion types, modality/quantifiers, links to affected amounts and obligations, and reviewed translation into constraints without inventing thresholds. | Specified Narrative/coverage records and modality rules in Ch. 3 and Core 0. Apple note and cross-reference obligations are retained; representative debt language is interpreted. Complete translation of all material narratives remains open. G2, G11. |\n58-| MC04 | Separate reported assertions, extraction readings, derivations, assumptions and conflicts. U1, U2, P, D. | Define source/derived/assumed status propagation and conflict handling; show both extraction error and a genuinely conflicting disclosure without silently changing either source. | Specified source/assumption constraints, review actions and conflict sets in Chs. 3, 6, 10. The 720-to-120 OCR repair differs from the 120-to-110 reported correction; transitive invalidation has a reference check. Bounded debt acceptance/source/assumption links are now checked; full workflow validation remains pending. G2, G15, G17. |\n59:| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\n60:| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\n61-| MC07 | Align differing company labels and overlapping dimensions without equating unlike measurements or double counting. U1, D. | Specify concept/mapping relationships, applicability and aggregation rules; demonstrate company extensions and product/geography totals over the same population. | Specified mapping composition, applicability and partition obligations in Ch. 3/Core 0. The product/channel overlap counterexample is checked; general company-extension/mapping validation awaits implementation. G2, G12. |\n62-\n63-## M2 — Histories, interpretation and uncertainty\n64-\n65-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\n--\n72-\n73-## M3 — Economic events, journals and forecasts\n74-\n75-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\n76-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n77:| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event preconditions and operations in Chs. 2, 8. Reference journals, atomic rejection and idempotency checks pass. This verifies the bounded oracle, not a production event engine or accounting compliance. G2, G4, G6. |\n78-| MC14 | Give scenarios and decision information explicit meanings. U2, P, D. | Define supported exogenous stress, observational-conditioning and intervention modes, or explicitly scope unsupported modes; enforce information dates and distinguish real-world from pricing measures. | Specified exogenous stress, observational conditioning, intervention preconditions and information capabilities in Ch. 8/Core 0. Finite conditioning, an information-date example and debt stress typing/provenance are checked; causal intervention execution and arbitrary information-policy enforcement remain pending. G6, G14. |\n79:| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\n80:| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\n81:| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\n82-| MC18 | Preserve joint conditional future outcomes, honest bounds and distinct failure/completeness states. U2, P, D. | Define result payloads and queries that retain branch/path dependence, distinguish sampled ranges from certified bounds and distinguish default from unsupported/numerically failed output without silent dropping or renormalisation. | Specified result cells, branch statuses, strict bound attainment and unresolved mass in Chs. 6, 8, 10/Core 0. Exact linear, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\n83-\n84-## M4 — Standards, sectors and company variation\n85-\n86-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\n87-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n88:| MC19 | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE with dated treatments, elections and transitions. U1, U3. | Define the supported treatment matrix, rule authority and version selection; show matched economic events under selected genuinely different treatments and identify unimplemented operations. | Partially repaired. Ch. 9 compares FIFO/LIFO/average and records dated rule selection. Selected IAS-equivalent paragraphs inspected in official AASB texts; US LIFO has company-policy evidence only, full ASC authority is blocked, and official ASBE version verification remains pending. Source dossiers record exact edition/period limits and correct Caterpillar inventories to Note 8. G7, G8, G13. The acquired panel now supplies report-level preparation-basis evidence across US GAAP, IFRS-oriented reporting and ASBE; this does not replace dated primary accounting authority. |\n89:| MC20 | Support materially different industry and company concepts without bypassing the common accounting semantics. U1, D. | Specify extension points, concept mappings and rule admissibility; include representative industry differences and an invalid company override. | Specified extension points, override admission, separate books and mappings in Chs. 3, 7, 9/Core 0. Inventory/bank/insurer structures expose distinct state requirements. Full invalid-override and package-conformance execution remains pending. G2, G7, G12. |\n90:| MC21 | Represent banks' liabilities, assets, deposits, capital and regulatory/economic constraints. U1, U2. | Define core bank structural records now and operation-level later methods for funding, credit, liquidity and capital, including accounting/prudential reconciliation and an appropriate worked case. | Partially repaired: Ch. 9 specifies bank origination, transfer, interest, allowance, cash funding and default; exact fixture balances and capital reconciliation pass. Prudential weights are illustrative; full allowance lifecycle, IFRS 9/CECL and jurisdictional capital rules remain open. G7, G8. |\n91:| MC22 | Represent insurers' contract groups, claims, service/finance components, assets and reinsurance. U1, U2. | Define cohort/group state and movements, declared measurement approaches and interfaces, reinsurance links and a complete structural/roll-forward example; expand actuarial/accounting support. | Partially repaired: Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` give a complete short-duration PAA gross/reinsurance roll-forward and chain-ladder point calculation. Selected AASB 17 paragraphs and Mack technical sections inspected. Separate treaty PAA eligibility and recognition timing are explicit in Version 1.2; journal counterexamples vary transferred risk and non-performance independently. General measurement, transition, variable fees and uncertainty/RA estimation remain open. G7, G8, G16. |\n92-\n93-## M5 — Concrete methods, DSL and implementation contracts\n94-\n95-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\n96-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n97-| MC23 | Explain the DSL's role and tradeoffs against credible alternatives, including typed ordinary code, XBRL, ledgers, rule languages and probabilistic tools. U1, U3, P. | Tie each claimed benefit to the same concrete tasks and shared semantic requirements; state costs and a fair authoring comparison protocol. Keep empirical superiority unclaimed until evaluated. | Specified shared-IR comparison and identical authoring tasks in Chs. 5, 11/Core 0; limited syntax/literal equivalence checked. Participant study, full frontend equivalence and any superiority claim remain unevaluated. G2, G9. |\n98-| MC24 | Specify the core language and IR completely enough for compatible independent implementations. U3, D. | Provide complete grammar/lexical rules, AST/IR schemas, types, context rules, built-ins, errors, package interfaces and source-to-IR-to-result fixtures, including the demonstration package. | Core 0 grammar, closed structural IR, built-ins, arities, context/domain rules and complete debt dependency package supplied. Authored expected IR and selected expression-to-result checks pass. A frozen 17-export registry and bounded debt static validator now pass positive and schema-valid negative cases. General compilation, package loading, remaining semantic conformance and independent implementability assessment remain open. G2, G12, G15. |\n99-| MC25 | Specify APIs, adapters, storage, versioning, identity and deterministic recovery. U3, P, D. | Define complete arguments/results, state ownership, migration semantics, evidence/model/run identity, event idempotency, random-stream allocation and replay requirements with examples. | Specified APIs, ownership, canonical identity, migration/replay and stream keying in Ch. 10/Core 0; concrete adapter exchanges included. Reference identity, replay/conflict, stream and bounded frozen-export integrity checks pass; transactional storage, migrations and non-Z3 adapters remain unimplemented. G2, G9, G18. |\n100-| MC26 | Specify supported numerical/solver operations and their limits. U3, P, D. | Define formula fragments, reformulations, exact/approximate monetary treatment, rounding, strict-domain bounds, infeasibility/conflict evidence, timeout and resource behaviour. | Specified rational-linear/finite-choice scope, amount reformulation, quantisation distinctions and typed unknowns in Ch. 6/Core 0. Z3 checks 4.975 attained and 7.035 unattained and concrete histories. Nonlinear solvers and a production rounding/optimization layer remain pending. G3, G10. |\n101-| MC27 | Specify analyst/LLM review and correction as a traceable local workflow. U1, U3, D. | Define proposal, acceptance, alternative, rejection and supersession actions, with evidence requirements, consistency checks and derived-result invalidation; show an actual conflict-resolution example. | Specified Propose/Accept/AcceptAlternative/Reject/Supersede actions, examples and dependency invalidation in Ch. 10/Core 0. The transitive invalidation oracle passes; a complete analyst UI/workflow and human adjudication remain pending. G2, G17. |\n102:| MC28 | Connect the full design through complete synthetic and real disclosure cases. U1, U2, U3, D. | Supply a known-history synthetic company and a named annual/interim real package across multiple dates; trace representative notes through records, constraints, alternatives and all affected future statements. Add structural finance/sector cases before fixing the core types. | Reference cases delivered in Ch. 2: complete synthetic Northstar history/revision/forecast and named Apple annual/interim inventory, notes and conditional stress. Ch. 9 supplies sector/finance structures. Real-company full semantic closure and independent case annotation remain open; no complete Apple forecast is claimed. G4, G5, G7. Nine eight-year report sequences are now source-checked; report-wide semantic cases and executable oracles remain to be prepared. |\n103-\n104-## M6 — Literature, sources and reusable software\n105-\n106-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\n107-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n108:| MC29 | Conduct a broad, technically grounded literature survey beyond the original collection. U3, P. | Inspect relevant primary methods/theory/evaluation/appendices and official code where available; compare direct alternatives; make genuine backward/forward screening, source-specific omissions, corrections and claim support inspectable. | Partially repaired: 179 individual title/metadata decisions across 194 occurrences/72 searches replace generic exclusions; generation rejects unscreened candidates. Mack and selected rule sources add inspected technical support. All-candidate full-text review and later module literature are not complete. G8. |\n109:| MC30 | Preserve the relevant source library and precise provenance. U3, P. | Archive accessible relevant papers under the required naming convention, retain exact versions/anchors, preserve original files, and document unavailable sources without relying on their uninspected claims. | 32 catalogued paper PDFs verified by hash/page count, with original collection preserved; Apple filings and selected standards archived separately. Version/authority limits and four blocked papers remain recorded. Mechanical integrity does not certify every technical claim. G8. The additional financial-report corpus preserves 244 original versions, source/index/discovery hashes and an append-only attempt history; 192 target slots pass source acceptance. |\n110-| MC31 | Survey open-source tools and define evidence-based reuse boundaries. U3, P, D. | Inspect official interfaces/licences, identify supported subsets, specify adapter exchanges and version assumptions, and separate inspected capabilities from later integration/performance evidence. | Inspected software snapshots/licences retained; Ch. 10/Core 0 specify typed exchanges, errors and concrete examples. Z3 is exercised. Arelle/ACTUS/QuantLib/Docling/ledger integrations and pinned deployment combinations remain pending. G9. |\n111-\n112-## M7 — Governing scholarly design\n113-\n114-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\n115-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n116:| MC32 | Deliver a detailed, readable LaTeX/PDF document that governs the intended implementation. U3, P. | Explain the whole problem, justify chosen methods, stage mathematical prerequisites, define supported behaviour and disclose open scope; connect derivations and sources to complete examples and interfaces. Preserve mathematical/source fidelity during revisions and inspect the rendered result. | Revised Version 1.2 candidate, 11 chapters plus two appendices, full cases and supporting normative files. Build, rendered inspection and baseline-preservation review are recorded in `review/author-review.md`. Human comprehension, domain review and independent implementability acceptance remain pending. G1, G2, G4, G5, G7, G10. |\n117-\n118-## M8 — Validation, completion and sustained direction\n119-\n120-| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\n121-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n--\n135-feedback does not require an accounting-firm engagement.\n136-\n137-U5 source acquisition is accepted: active panel v2 contains all 192 target\n138-reports, with eight consecutive complete years for each of nine issuers.\n139-Henkel and Munich Re replace two inaccessible interim series under the reviewed\n140:plan; v1 evidence remains preserved. This advances MC01, MC03, MC05, MC19–22,\n141:MC28, MC30 and MC33–35 without closing semantic, accounting or forecast\n142-requirements. The [corpus result](accounting-benchmark-corpus-results.md),\n143-`data/financial-report-benchmark/coverage.json` and matching independent\n144-`integrity-manifest.json` preserve acceptance. Filing dates are evidenced for\n145-56 reports; 136 publication dates remain unverified. Counts are not accuracy scores.\n146-\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
