orts, including revisions, complex groups, unusual financing and sector-specific cases. Acquire additional reports only for demonstrated gaps. | A task-by-case coverage matrix that distinguishes absent, present and not inspected. Difficult cases are not yet inventoried; their absence has not been established. |\ndocs/design/review/consolidated-gap-solutions-2026-10-02.md:391:| Governing design and reader comprehension — MC32 | Incorporate validated method/case changes into the LaTeX argument, preserve equations and source qualifications, and inspect the rendered result. Test comprehension and independent implementability separately; author checks and compilation do not establish either. Continue provisional internal improvement while feedback is pending. |\ndocs/design/review/consolidated-gap-solutions-2026-10-02.md:392:| Traceability and resumability — MC34 | Keep MC01–MC35, G1–G18, source versions, implemented scope, unresolved decisions and next actions connected. Update current registers/reset notes after meaningful changes; preserve historical results and frozen release hashes. A plan, implemented feature, checked accounting method and validated forecast require distinct statuses. |\ndocs/design/review/consolidated-gap-solutions-2026-10-02.md:402:| Report identity, consolidation perimeter and accounting basis | G12, G7, G11 |\ndocs/design/review/consolidated-gap-solutions-2026-10-02.md:426:4. **Expand supported methods and integrations.** Add source-backed corporate,\ndocs/design/review/consolidated-gap-solutions-2026-10-02.md:450:This update consolidates known residuals, solutions and completion evidence.\ndocs/design/review/consolidated-gap-solutions-2026-10-02.md:452:register and leaves historical repair results and pinned corpus-release\ndocs/design/research/software/openfisca_openfisca-core-README.md:9:[![Newsletter](https://img.shields.io/badge/newsletter-subscribe!-informational.svg?style=for-the-badge)](mailto:contact%40openfisca.org?subject=Subscribe%2